WEBVTT

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:05.112
Open "Trip details" for the full picture of every trip on the line.

00:00:05.112 --> 00:00:10.920
The calendar tab goes trip by trip — report, time away from base, block, duty periods —

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:17.661
and an hour-by-hour chart you can tap for the pairing's own details, hotel and pickup times included.

00:00:18.361 --> 00:00:25.864
Each trip gets its own score for you, so you can see which trip is carrying a line and which one's dragging it down.

00:00:26.564 --> 00:00:35.651
The rest plan suggests when to sleep on each layover, worked out from when you'll get to the hotel and what your body clock will be doing.

00:00:36.351 --> 00:00:38.976
The body-clock score runs from 1 to 100 —

00:00:38.976 --> 00:00:44.930
the higher, the easier on you. Tap it to see exactly what costs points on that trip, and why.

00:00:45.630 --> 00:00:49.277
The score breakdown shows why the line scored what it did —

00:00:49.277 --> 00:00:54.716
what's working for you and what isn't — and the route tab maps where the line takes you.

